  "published": "2026-11-24",
  "updated": "2026-11-24",
  "intro": "QuickBooks Online, FreshBooks, Zoho Books, Wave and FreeAgent are five Xero alternatives with published pricing for small business accounting. Published list prices run from free tiers up to $340 a month on QuickBooks Online Advanced, and they differ in user limits, client or invoice caps and payroll add-ons.\n\nAt The Modern Wallet, we compare published business accounting fees so you can see how monthly subscriptions, invoice limits and per-worker payroll fees add up over twelve months. [Xero](https://www.xero.com/us/pricing-plans/) sells three plans in United States dollars (USD): Early at $27 a month, Growing at $59 a month and Established at $97 a month. The alternatives price differently: QuickBooks Online prices by plan tier with seat caps, FreshBooks prices by billable client counts, Zoho Books prices by annual invoice counts with user limits, Wave pairs a free tier with card fees, and FreeAgent charges a flat fee for sole proprietors.\n\nFor broader context on small business tools, see our [roundup of accounting software for freelancers](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/) and the [side-by-side comparison hub](/compare/). If you want dedicated breakdowns of other accounting systems, explore our [QuickBooks alternatives](/alternatives/quickbooks/), [FreshBooks alternatives](/alternatives/freshbooks/), and [Wave alternatives](/alternatives/wave/) guides.",
